  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This idea is mainly for people who purchase SDK3 avatars from Booth, VKET, or other sources, but aren't very familiar with Unity on a whole.\nFor it to work the avatar descriptor would have a section where you can specify what parameters are active by default when you upload an avatar.\nFor example:\n1) The user sets the avatar to always load in on the Green color scheme, as opposed to the default Blue.\n2) The user sets the avatar to always load in on the dark skinned setting, rather than the light skinned one.\nWhile you can just change the default layer state on the FX layer to do that, there is an issue where in game it will not realize the default layer has been switched. So in this case the hair and skintone are on the same material, and you attempted to switch the hair color in game, it will reset to the default skintone instead of your preferred one.\nSpecifying parameters through the descriptor means the game will understand that \"skintone = 2\" is active, and take that into account when choosing which hair color animation it switches to in game.\nThis will also make it easier for creators to optimize while still offering many options, as having separate materials for hair/eyes/skintone just to prevent this kind of thing from happening piles on the drawcalls quickly.",
